5. SIGNATURE STAMP ANIMATION
============================

This is the most important animation in the application.

When a new eligible stamp is successfully awarded by the backend, animate the corresponding stamp slot.

ANIMATION SEQUENCE:

PHASE 1 — PAGE ARRIVAL

* Fade the loyalty card into view.
* Slightly scale the card from 96% to 100%.
* Use a gentle spring-like transition.
* Reveal the stamp slots in sequence.

PHASE 2 — ACTIVE STAMP HIGHLIGHT

* Highlight the newly earned stamp slot.
* Add a soft warm glow.
* Create a subtle circular ripple behind the slot.
* Slightly enlarge the slot.

PHASE 3 — STAMP DROP

* A small bakery-themed stamp icon drops from above.
* Use a smooth ease-in animation.
* Add a very subtle rotation.
* The stamp settles naturally into the correct slot.

PHASE 4 — TICK MARK REVEAL

* Draw or animate a beautiful checkmark.
* The tick should appear as if it is being drawn.
* Use SVG stroke-dasharray and stroke-dashoffset or a suitable animation technique.
* Add a small bounce when the tick completes.
* Show a subtle gold sparkle.

PHASE 5 — PROGRESS UPDATE

Animate the progress counter.

Example:

Before: 2 / 5 STAMPS

After: 3 / 5 STAMPS

The number should smoothly count up.

PHASE 6 — CELEBRATION

Display a subtle message:

"Yay! Another sweet moment collected! 🍰"

Add a few delicate sparkles or small confetti particles.

Keep the celebration short, elegant, and lightweight.

Do not make the animation interfere with navigation.

Do not replay the new-stamp animation every time the customer refreshes the page.

Persist the stamp state in the database.

Use a unique stamp-event identifier and an idempotent animation trigger.

If the customer opens an already-redeemed link, display the completed stamp immediately with a gentle entrance animation instead of replaying the entire stamp-drop sequence.

Respect the device's reduced-motion setting.

The application must remain responsive on low-end Android phones.

